# A copy of a spell is not cast, but it copies the alternative cost the original was cast for (CR 707.10): a copy of a
# sneak-cast spell had its sneak cost paid too. Bot1 sneaks The Last Ronin's Technique in (Mox Pearl and a Plains) with the
# Ornithopter returned, and with it on the stack casts Lutri, the Spellchaser (flash), whose enters trigger copies it. The
# copy resolves first: three tapped tokens attacking Bot2. The original then makes three more, and the six deal 6 combat
# damage (Bot2 at 14).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
The Last Ronin's Technique
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Hand.The Last Ronin's Technique.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Hand.Lutri, the Spellchaser.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ninja Turtle Spirit Token#4.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ninja Turtle Spirit Token#1.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ninja Turtle Spirit Token#1.Token = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 9
